///1SUBMIT
Help by Willem Aandewiel
SUBMIT - Execute a file of CP/M commands

///2SYNTAX
SUBMIT name arguments
Reads name.SUB and substitutes parameters such as $1 and $2.

///2EXAMPLE
BUILD.SUB may contain:

  ASM $1
  DIR $1.*

On a writable A: containing ASM and the required source:

  A>SUBMIT BUILD DEMO

This example assembles DEMO without running the result.

///2DISKS
The original SUBMIT creates $$$.SUB for the CCP.
The standard CCP processes the submitted commands through A:.
A read-only A: is therefore unsuitable for that standard workflow.
Use a suitable writable system environment or the modified
SUBMIT/CCP procedure supplied with your installation.

///2INPUT
Ordinary SUBMIT supplies commands to CP/M.
XSUB extends this to line input for interactive programs.
Automate LOAD only when assembly errors are being checked.
